  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F001-AL9" ;
  triage:title "Unnecessary pub export of ReplacementReceivedHookSelector — narrow re-export to the factory fn" ;
  triage:description "ruthless-boundary-qa (AL9-QA-1, 2026-08-07, re-verified against confirmed-clean tree) flags that ReplacementReceivedHookSelector is exported as pub from its module in crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/received_hook_selector.rs, when only the factory function that constructs it needs to be part of the public surface. Minor boundary-tightening finding, not a defect. RECHECK (QA-AL9-RECHECK-1, 2026-08-07): does not reproduce at integrate/phase-al@dc9c7197. `struct ReplacementReceivedHookSelector` (line 71) carries no `pub` keyword; only the factory function `active_received_hook_selector` (line 27) is public. Fix commit 221f0f93 ('fix(AL9): hide concrete received hook selector') predates this finding's filing -- the AL9-QA-1 review that filed this finding appears to have evaluated a stale snapshot of the branch. Confirmed independently by quality-mgr via direct file read, not taken on arch-ctm's self-report alone." ;
